  "algorithm_steps": [
   "INPUT MODEL: std::stoi(const std::string&) here receives the raw bytes of argv[2] (NUL-terminated C string, arbitrary non-UTF-8 bytes allowed). Operate on a byte slice (&[u8]), not a &str. The program never calls setlocale, so the C locale is active and env vars LC_ALL/LC_NUMERIC/LANG have ZERO effect (verified).",
   "STEP 0 (guard, outside stoi): The call only happens when argc > 1 AND bytes(argv[1]) == b\"--a\". Otherwise count stays 15 and argv[2] is never touched. If argv[1] == \"--a\" but argv[2] is absent (argc == 2), the std::string parameter is constructed from a NULL pointer, which throws std::logic_error BEFORE stoi runs: stderr gets exactly \"terminate called after throwing an instance of 'std::logic_error'\\n  what():  basic_string::_S_construct null not valid\\n\" and the process dies by SIGABRT (shell-visible exit 134).",
   "STEP 1 (skip leading whitespace): Advance past a run of zero or more bytes in EXACTLY this set: 0x20 space, 0x09 tab, 0x0A newline, 0x0B vertical tab, 0x0C form feed, 0x0D carriage return. Nothing else is whitespace: byte 0xA0 (NBSP), UTF-8 U+00A0, U+2000, U+3000 (ideographic space), U+FEFF (BOM), and 0x7F all FAIL to be skipped and cause invalid_argument (all verified).",
   "STEP 2 (optional single sign): If the next byte is 0x2B ('+') or 0x2D ('-'), consume exactly ONE such byte and record the sign. Do NOT allow a second sign and do NOT allow whitespace between the sign and the digits: \"--1\", \"++1\", \"+-1\", \"-+1\", \"- 1\", \"-  1\", \" + 1\" all throw invalid_argument (verified).",
   "STEP 3 (require at least one digit): The next byte must be an ASCII digit 0x30..0x39. If it is not, no conversion occurred: throw the invalid_argument error. This covers \"\", \" \", \"\\t\", \"\\n\", \"\\r\", \"\\v\", \"\\f\", pure-whitespace strings, \"-\", \"+\", \"x\", \"abc\", \".5\", \",5\", and ALL non-ASCII digits (Arabic-Indic '\\u{0663}', fullwidth '\\u{ff13}', superscript '\\u{b2}', '\\u{bd}', Roman numeral '\\u{2163}') — verified.",
   "STEP 4 (base is fixed 10): There is NO prefix detection whatsoever. No 0x/0X hex: \"0x1\" == 0, \"0x10\" == 0, \"0X1A\" == 0, \"-0x10\" == 0 (parse stops at 'x'/'X'). No octal: \"08\" and \"09\" and \"0008\" parse successfully as decimal 8, 9, 8 — if base were 8 they would have yielded 0 (verified, this definitively rules out octal). Leading zeros are simply insignificant digits; any number of them is fine (\"0000001\" == 1, 5000 zeros == 0, 5000 zeros followed by '1' == 1).",
   "STEP 5 (consume maximal ASCII digit run): Read the longest possible run of bytes in 0x30..0x39 and accumulate value = value * 10 + digit. Accumulate in a WIDER type than i32 (i64, mirroring LP64 `long` used by the underlying strtol), or track overflow explicitly. Saturate rather than wrap if the run is astronomically long (5000 nines must not wrap into a plausible-looking value).",
